# Evaluation of Teaching and Learning Processes in a Computer-Supported Mechanical Engineering Course.

**Authors:** Brown, Alan

## Abstract
Evaluates the teaching and learning processes in a computer-supported first-year undergraduate course in the Department of Mechanical Engineering at the University of Surrey (England). Students saw the workshop delivery as being more interesting, effective, and efficient than lecture-based delivery; help from the tutor was seen as the most valuable type of support. (AEF)

